<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext (plain http) is for the local network only. Everything on the internet is https.

  What Android can and can't express here: a domain-config matches exact host names and their
  subdomains. It has no address ranges, so it can't say "192.168.0.0/16". A home Beebo on the
  LAN is reached at whatever address the router handed out (http://192.168.1.50:47811,
  http://10.0.0.7:47811, a Tailscale 100.x address), so the base config has to permit
  cleartext, and the app narrows it in code instead:

    core/CleartextPolicy.Guard, a network interceptor on every OkHttp client the app builds
    (API, posters, the player, subtitles, downloads, hub, beebo.tv, account deletion), refuses a
    plain-http request - or a redirect - to anything but loopback, 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16,
    100.64/10 (Tailscale), link-local, IPv6 local addresses and local-only names (.local, .lan,
    a single-label name). The only WebView (Campsite games) loads 127.0.0.1 and refuses to
    navigate anywhere else.

  Beebo's own internet hosts are locked to https here as well, so no code path can ever reach
  them in plain text. usesCleartextTraffic was removed from the manifest: with this file
  present it is ignored on every Android version the app supports (minSdk 24).

  Casting away from home (player/PhoneCastRelay) needs NOTHING added here, and nothing was.
  In that case the phone is the SERVER: a Chromecast on the same Wi-Fi fetches
  http://<this phone>:<port>/c/<token>/<slot> from it. Android's network security config governs
  what this app CONNECTS OUT to, not what connects in, so an incoming plain-http request is not
  its business at all. The two outgoing legs are already covered: the phone fetches the film from
  https://name.beebo.tv over the tunnel, and the only plain-http URL the app itself may load is
  the poster on its own 192.168.x.x address, which the base config permits and CleartextPolicy
  narrows to private addresses exactly as it does for a home Beebo on the LAN. Nothing about
  cleartext was loosened for the app as a whole.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">beebo.tv</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">beebotv.com</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">beeboentertainment.com</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
